@anon.53fe85e3a453dfbf0ab1e8743506e67c.1353 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [487 x i8] }> <{ [487 x i8] c"A whole number.\0A\0AThe number can be negative, zero, or positive. As Typst uses 64 bits to\0Astore integers, integers cannot be smaller than `{-9223372036854775808}` or\0Alarger than `{9223372036854775807}`.\0A\0AThe number can also be specified as hexadecimal, octal, or binary by\0Astarting it with a zero followed by either `x`, `o`, or `b`.\0A\0AYou can convert a value to an integer with this type's constructor.\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0A#(1 + 2) \\\0A#(2 - 5) \\\0A#(3 + 4 < 8)\0A\0A#0xff \\\0A#0o10 \\\0A#0b1001\0A```" }>, align 1
